 "frozen_rule_text": "Within each declaration date, order executable treatment rows by their already-frozen liquidity rank and ticker. Match the first treatment slot to the one actual same-date cash-feasible core slot when present and not the same ticker; otherwise match it to cash. Match every additional treatment slot to cash. A core slot and its return may be consumed at most once. A same-ticker treatment/core collision is matched to cash and may not manufacture replacement value against itself.",
 "allocation_order_contract": "Declaration dates are processed in ascending order; within a declaration date treatment rows are ordered by (frozen liquidity rank, ticker). Only the first ordinal may consume a core slot. Core slot candidates for one entry session are ordered by (entry_date, core_slot_id); the first non-same-ticker, not-yet-consumed slot is matched. Every unmatched, additional, collision, or consumed case is cash. A core_slot_id is consumed globally at most once across the whole roster.",
 "same_date_semantics": "same-date means the treatment row's own entry session (first canonical session strictly after declaration_date) equals the core trade's entry_date, matching the exp-20260728-006 precedent of same-session core comparison",
